            "actions": []
          },
          "teach": {
            "id": "teach",
            "text": "The shadows here are not empty — they are filled with echoes of the dead. I can teach you to shape them into a ward. Focus your will, and the echoes will shield you.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "TEACH_SPELL",
                "target": "shadow_ward",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Lorekeeper Iris teaches you the Shadow Ward spell.",
                "value": "GOOD",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "lore": {
            "id": "lore",
            "text": "Umbryn was the first to remember. Before him, death was the end. He made death merely a transition — from living to remembered. The Archive is his gift and his curse. Every soul that passes through the world leaves an echo here. Umbryn hears them all.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "That is a heavy burden.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell",
                "conditions": []
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "farewell": {
            "id": "farewell",
            "text": "May the echoes guide you, traveler. The Archive forgets nothing.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "chronicler_offer": {
            "id": "chronicler_offer",
            "text": "A standing wave. Ten years of readings and there is one resonance at the northern ward-circle that has not moved, not by a hair, through every collapse and every rebuilding.\nEverything else out there is an echo. An echo decays. That is the definition; that is what makes it an echo. This one does not decay, which means it is not a memory of somebody. It is somebody.\nHooded. Studies the wards. The locals call it The Chronicler and give it directions, cheerfully, like it is a lost traveller, and it has been standing there since before the Archive was built.\nI am not brave enough to ask it what it is. You go and ask it. Then come back and tell me whether I should have.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll go and ask.",
                "nextNodeId": "chronicler_accept",
                "conditions": []
              },
              {
                "label": "Some things are better unasked.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell",
                "conditions": []
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "chronicler_accept": {
            "id": "chronicler_accept",
            "text": "North. The ward-circle above the Archive gate. And Traveller — if it answers you by name, do not answer back.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_QUEST",
                "target": "the_one_who_stayed_awake",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "stayed_awake_offered",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Quest accepted: The One Who Stayed Awake",
                "value": "GOOD",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "chronicler_done": {
            "id": "chronicler_done",
            "text": "It talked to you about crystals. [She laughs, once, badly.] Of course it did. Ten years of standing wave and it gives directions to Dusthaven.\nThat is what it does. That is all it has done. Whatever it was, it stayed awake through the Shattering and everything after, and the only thing it has found to do with four hundred years of consciousness is help strangers find the archivist.\nI think that is the most frightening thing I have ever learned and I cannot explain why, and I think I will be explaining it to myself for the rest of my life.\n...I am glad I did not ask. Thank you for asking.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "stayed_awake_done",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "ADD_FAVOR",
                "target": "UMBRYN",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 5
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "iris_day": {
            "id": "iris_day",
            "text": "A day when nothing happened. [She is quiet long enough that you think she has refused.]\nThe morning before the Shattering. I was in the lower stacks re-shelving a run of tide-tables that had been shelved wrong by somebody who has been dead for four centuries, and I was annoyed about it, and I had a very good pear.\nI have never told anyone that. Everyone wants the afternoon. Nobody has ever once asked me about the morning.\n[She writes it out, slowly, in a hand trained on catastrophes.] Tell Mord the pear was the best thing that has ever happened to me and I did not notice at the time. He will understand that. It is his entire argument.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "ordinary_day",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "day_iris",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
